{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Escaping slashes in can leave regex expressions difficult to read.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/37d5705799d4c5d5f91688d88381823c7f6ce01978a371893a0ea643718218cc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.86], [2, 0.86, 1.16], [3, 1.16, 1.44], [4, 1.44, 1.64], [6, 2.06, 2.5], [7, 2.5, 3.04], [8, 3.04, 3.36], [9, 3.36, 3.58]]}, {"text": "A regex statement that is meant to identify a url like this one http://atdc.org/wp-admin/admin-ajax.php.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/850d7ed43b772ae17194d271a442755c511c551680d869f1b1ebbb86a6c49398.mp3"}, {"text": "would look something like this using the standard /expression/ notation:", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e363e6fe565cbdab48ea95384119e9638e9fb8bde9bb12a0873adc1e4267aeb5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.56], [7, 1.56, 1.98], [9, 3.02, 3.52]]}, {"text": "But if you use the %r{expression} notation, then your regex expressions do not need to be muddled with escaping slashes:", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bb8b93eb8c46c86b776255ed0fea0c12546f5bd66563b6a4e572ba7d005ecab7.mp3"}, {"text": "Much easier to read :)", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/88388cd6158e9b64235fa8294006d41c64f099163f6166b52a6ff6fc3265f24b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.68], [2, 0.68, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.14]]}]}